# Quests: generated by tools/quests/make_quests.py, edit there
betterquesting.questline.7dZOq4U1Vfa2Yr9apUvsiQ.name=Better Communications
betterquesting.questline.7dZOq4U1Vfa2Yr9apUvsiQ.desc=Telephones on pylon lines, radios, mobile phones and satellites, carried by voice chat.
betterquesting.quest.IHTr1EMRVx6vQQ7722eirw.name=Wired for Sound
betterquesting.quest.IHTr1EMRVx6vQQ7722eirw.desc=Everything starts with a wire. Phone Cable is red alloy wire in rubber, made in the assembler. It joins a Telephone to a Line Terminal, up to 32 blocks of it, and loses nothing on the way.
betterquesting.quest.b14IecXxXxuWU8oeGOPcNw.name=Ring, Ring
betterquesting.quest.b14IecXxXxuWU8oeGOPcNw.desc=A Telephone: a circuit, a note block for the bell and a steel body, assembled with a cord of Phone Cable. Right-click it to pick up the handset. It's yours, and its six-digit number is too.
betterquesting.quest.mXRjCMiFWsyGTG0Id2bbig.name=End of the Line
betterquesting.quest.mXRjCMiFWsyGTG0Id2bbig.desc=Every line starts and ends at a Line Terminal. It runs on 4 EU/t of LV power, serves exactly one phone on its cable, and links to one Pylon Head: wrench the terminal, then the head.
betterquesting.quest._OpArmItVHW8jB5_z18yig.name=Up on the Pole
betterquesting.quest._OpArmItVHW8jB5_z18yig.desc=A Pylon Head on top of a column of 6 to 16 Steel Frame Boxes carries the line. Two pylons link up to four times the shorter one's height apart, as long as nothing solid is in the way. Pylons need no power and keep working unloaded. The line loses signal with every block: plan a repeater at least every 225 blocks.
betterquesting.quest._xekW5q3V6-D2yESxW4Bqw.name=Hello? Can You Hear Me?
betterquesting.quest._xekW5q3V6-D2yESxW4Bqw.desc=Two Telephones, each on its own Line Terminal, and pylons between them. Pick up the handset: with only one other phone on the line it rings straight away, otherwise dial a number or pick a contact. Make a call that connects. A Telephone call is narrow and gritty, but it carries your voice as far as the line goes.
betterquesting.quest.EwUn7B5YXiqaZtu5vTGc2Q.name=Keeping the Signal Alive
betterquesting.quest.EwUn7B5YXiqaZtu5vTGc2Q.desc=A Repeater Head is a Pylon Head that regenerates the signal, so line loss starts over after it. It takes 4 EU/t of LV power from a cable on any side, and works only while loaded and powered.
betterquesting.quest.ARn2PctkVOe0cqI7997r1Q.name=Switchboard
betterquesting.quest.ARn2PctkVOe0cqI7997r1Q.desc=A plain line joins exactly two phones. A Router Head has 15 link slots and turns lines into a network, where any phone can dial any other. It regenerates the signal like a repeater, and takes 16 EU/t of LV power from a cable.
betterquesting.quest.UYdKN4lyUKWOiqsyX6luCQ.name=On the Air
betterquesting.quest.UYdKN4lyUKWOiqsyX6luCQ.desc=An Antenna T1 head sits on a mast of 4 to 32 Steel Frame Boxes, over a 3x3 base of LV Machine Casings with an Energy Hatch, and uses 32 EU/t. It reaches about 64 blocks on open ground; height helps, and hills and roofs cost signal. Antennas link to each other on their own. Wrench one to a Pylon Head or Line Terminal within 16 blocks to carry that line over radio.
betterquesting.quest.VdecT0iBUsCxBEbIo6xNeA.name=Base Station
betterquesting.quest.VdecT0iBUsCxBEbIo6xNeA.desc=A Transceiver is a radio on a block, at MV and 32 EU/t. Stand within 2 blocks of it and hold the radio push-to-talk key, Caps Lock unless you changed it, to talk on its channel. Its loudspeaker plays the channel to everyone within 16 blocks. On its own it reaches about 125 blocks on open ground.
betterquesting.quest.8sQY72VCXU2ZURqIKp1zVw.name=Reading the Air
betterquesting.quest.8sQY72VCXU2ZURqIKp1zVw.desc=Hold a Signal Analyzer to see your radio signal: its strength in dB, its level, the antenna serving you, and what costs the most, whether distance, terrain, cover, weather or noise. A link needs 6 dB for Low and 12 for Medium. Below 4 it cuts out at once; between 4 and 6 it holds for 3 seconds, then drops.
betterquesting.quest.82uwmy_wU3eMPoGqyurVlw.name=Pocket Radio
betterquesting.quest.82uwmy_wU3eMPoGqyurVlw.desc=A Walkie-Talkie runs on its own MV battery: charge it like any GT tool. Right-click to pick one of 16 channels or switch it off, or sneak and scroll to change channel. Hold push-to-talk to transmit. It reaches about 80 blocks on its own and much further through antennas, and anyone within 6 blocks hears what it receives.
betterquesting.quest.gNOxxRElWUebInHOkYOeQw.name=Over and Out
betterquesting.quest.gNOxxRElWUebInHOkYOeQw.desc=Talk to someone over the radio, or hear them: on a walkie, through a Transceiver, or through the antennas between you. Channels are open to anyone tuned in. When two people talk at once, each listener hears the stronger one.
betterquesting.quest.BRsUHvwqVhSei0mx4y1eWg.name=A Taller Mast
betterquesting.quest.BRsUHvwqVhSei0mx4y1eWg.desc=An Antenna T2 stands on MV Machine Casings with an Aluminium Frame Box mast and uses 128 EU/t. It reaches about 128 blocks, twice a T1: every 6 dB of link budget doubles the range on open ground. Antennas repeat all 16 radio channels between them, and carry calls between the lines bridged onto them.
betterquesting.quest.fia8emGdXIqzunSxVhLBng.name=Across the Valley
betterquesting.quest.fia8emGdXIqzunSxVhLBng.desc=An Antenna T3 stands on HV Machine Casings with a Stainless Steel Frame Box mast and uses 512 EU/t. It reaches about 256 blocks. Build it high: it surveys the land around it every five minutes, and a hill in the way can cost more than the distance.
betterquesting.quest.Cs4eUVpnUBeevZzOvcInrw.name=Face to Face
betterquesting.quest.Cs4eUVpnUBeevZzOvcInrw.desc=A Videophone is a speakerphone with a screen, at MV and 32 EU/t. Give it Phone Cable to a Line Terminal, like a Telephone. Right-click it to dial, answer or hang up. Everyone within 4 blocks is in its call and on its screen, and its loudspeaker carries the call 16 blocks. It hangs up by itself 30 seconds after the last person walks away.
betterquesting.quest.1e_b8ZF0VRq1STROZstNIg.name=Seeing Is Believing
betterquesting.quest.1e_b8ZF0VRq1STROZstNIg.desc=See someone in a video call: on a Videophone, a Mobile Phone or an ME Phone, with their front camera on. The front camera shows your character, and the rear camera what you see, in calls of two people at High or better. Video needs Medium: at Low the picture freezes and the voice carries on. The phone screen's Video tab shows the call full size and switches each camera.
betterquesting.quest.tmuzvF6QVE-ZigvcfAhM5Q.name=Phone in Your Pocket
betterquesting.quest.tmuzvF6QVE-ZigvcfAhM5Q.desc=A Mobile Phone gets its service from antennas, on the calls band: about 64 blocks from a T1 on open ground, twice that from a T2. It takes its number when you first use it, and works from your inventory or a bauble slot. Its battery holds 1,200,000 EU and drains 4 EU/t on standby, 16 in a call. The Phone key, N unless you changed it, answers, hangs up, or opens its screen.
betterquesting.quest.QTf-qLjuX5uncRhFsloOcg.name=Can You Hear Me Now?
betterquesting.quest.QTf-qLjuX5uncRhFsloOcg.desc=Make or take a call on a Mobile Phone. Its bars show your service while you hold it. Rain costs a phone 3 dB of its service, a thunderstorm 6, and an antenna's screen maps where its signal reaches. In a call, add more phones from the keypad: up to 8 people talk together.
betterquesting.quest.SSBYl-CuVHeaS00Zgy5NWA.name=Wireless Everywhere
betterquesting.quest.SSBYl-CuVHeaS00Zgy5NWA.desc=An ME Phone is a Mobile Phone with an ME network's link. Link it at a Security Terminal, like a Wireless Terminal: it has service at Max wherever that network's wireless access points reach, boosters included, and charges in an ME charger. ME Phones on one ME network call each other with no antenna.
betterquesting.quest.6JNs0PJ2W_2dWPcb8B5q0A.name=Bridging the Networks
betterquesting.quest.6JNs0PJ2W_2dWPcb8B5q0A.desc=An ME Bridge joins an ME network to a BeCom network, so ME Phones can call any phone. Put it on ME cable, where it takes one channel, and wrench-link it to a BeCom node within 16 blocks. It uses 512 EU/t.
betterquesting.quest.1FYiW9xFV5eNdWDcFL6cbw.name=Long Distance
betterquesting.quest.1FYiW9xFV5eNdWDcFL6cbw.desc=Call a phone outside your ME network from an ME Phone, through an ME Bridge: a Telephone on a line, a Mobile Phone, or a Videophone.
betterquesting.quest.oNm-cIc3Xoy6hejGu6UM7Q.name=Through the Portal
betterquesting.quest.oNm-cIc3Xoy6hejGu6UM7Q.desc=A Portal Relay works within 4 blocks of a Nether portal, an End portal, a Twilight Forest portal or a Personal Space portal, on 32 EU/t of MV power. Wrench-link it to an antenna, a Pylon Head or a Line Terminal of your network. Then wrench it, go through the portal, and wrench a relay on the other side within 5 minutes: the pair joins the two networks at High.
betterquesting.quest.78j3bHKHWF6_v27ljQ8cYg.name=Payload
betterquesting.quest.78j3bHKHWF6_v27ljQ8cYg.desc=A Satellite is an HV emitter and sensor with two solar panels. Put it on Galacticraft's Tier 1 rocket parts in the assembler to make a Satellite Rocket. It doesn't fly from Galacticraft's pads: it needs a Satellite Launch Pad.
betterquesting.quest.CW6Vyi4yXYClMf9my2HQKQ.name=Liftoff
betterquesting.quest.CW6Vyi4yXYClMf9my2HQKQ.desc=The Satellite Launch Pad is a 5 by 5 floor of Clean Stainless Steel Machine Casings under open sky, with an input bus for rockets, an input hatch for rocket fuel, an energy hatch and a maintenance hatch. A launch takes 30 s at 480 EU/t and 1,000 L of fuel, and puts a satellite into orbit over the pad's dimension.
betterquesting.quest.J3UFmY7aUkyD5jAJI7lDBw.name=A Constellation
betterquesting.quest.J3UFmY7aUkyD5jAJI7lDBw.desc=With 5 satellites over a dimension, every phone and radio under its open sky gets a signal from them, at Low; 14 give Medium, 37 High and 100 Max. A roof weakens it, and rain costs a few dB. Satellites come down after about 100 days, so keep launching.
betterquesting.quest.aEl8W97yVGeFRBy0p4O4ZA.name=Dish Network
betterquesting.quest.aEl8W97yVGeFRBy0p4O4ZA.desc=A Satellite Dish joins its network to every other dish in the same dimension, through the satellites. It's a 5 by 5 dish of Clean Stainless Steel Machine Casings on a stand of three Stainless Steel Frame Boxes, with an energy hatch and a maintenance hatch, under open sky, on 512 EU/t. Wrench-link it to an antenna, a Pylon Head or a Line Terminal. Each maintenance problem costs it 2 dB.
betterquesting.quest.iphLiVwwUKakj8QR4PH2-w.name=Calling Home
betterquesting.quest.iphLiVwwUKakj8QR4PH2-w.desc=A Rocket Radio Receiver in the cargo of a rocket standing on a launch pad on a planet makes the rocket an antenna there, and the planet's link to the Overworld's satellites, at High. The rocket needs chests to have cargo. In the Overworld, phones under open sky and networks with a dish reach it.
betterquesting.quest.Ww6rBsobWMmbyc-M1rYILg.name=Out of This World
betterquesting.quest.Ww6rBsobWMmbyc-M1rYILg.desc=Call someone in another dimension: through a pair of Portal Relays to the Nether, the End, the Twilight Forest or a personal dimension, or through the Overworld's satellites to a planet with a Rocket Radio Receiver.
# End of quests

